{"uid":"756fd64918b1ed59","name":"test_a_rejected_write_leaves_no_row","fullName":"tests.db.test_claim_persistence#test_a_rejected_write_leaves_no_row","time":{"start":1789890797088,"stop":1789890797098,"duration":10},"description":"DB-CLM-006 - a 422 must not leave a partial record behind.\n\n    The failure mode being guarded against is a handler that inserts first and\n    validates second. The API would still return an error, so no API test could\n    detect it, while the database quietly accumulated invalid rows.\n\n    **Scoped to this test's own marker, and the first version was not.** It\n    compared a global ``count(*) WHERE status = 'DRAFT'`` before and after, which\n    failed two runs in three under ``-n 4``: other workers legitimately create\n    draft claims in between, so the number moves for reasons that have nothing to\n    do with this test.\n\n    That is the same error as the Phase 6 pagination flake, made again in a new\n    layer - which is the argument for stating the rule as a rule rather than\n    fixing instances of it. **A test may assert on an invariant globally, because\n    an invariant holds no matter who else is writing. It may never assert on an\n    aggregate globally, because an aggregate is a fact about the whole database\n    and the whole database is shared.**\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>DB-CLM-006 - a 422 must not leave a partial record behind.</p>\n<pre><code>The failure mode being guarded against is a handler that inserts first and\nvalidates second. The API would still return an error, so no API test could\ndetect it, while the database quietly accumulated invalid rows.\n\n**Scoped to this test's own marker, and the first version was not.** It\ncompared a global ``count(*) WHERE status = 'DRAFT'`` before and after, which\nfailed two runs in three under ``-n 4``: other workers legitimately create\ndraft claims in between, so the number moves for reasons that have nothing to\ndo with this test.\n\nThat is the same error as the Phase 6 pagination flake, made again in a new\nlayer - which is the argument for stating the rule as a rule rather than\nfixing instances of it. **A test may assert on an invariant globally, because\nan invariant holds no matter who else is writing. It may never assert on an\naggregate globally, because an aggregate is a fact about the whole database\nand the whole database is shared.**\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_verify_url","time":{"start":1789890794738,"stop":1789890794738,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"pytestconfig","time":{"start":1789890794738,"stop":1789890794738,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_session_faker","time":{"start":1789890794738,"stop":1789890794777,"duration":39},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"base_url","time":{"start":1789890794738,"stop":1789890794738,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"delete_output_dir","time":{"start":1789890794738,"stop":1789890794738,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_framework_logging","time":{"start":1789890794777,"stop":1789890794778,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"paramete